WEBVTT

00:09:29.430 --> 00:09:31.080
communicating remotely with them.

00:09:31.990 --> 00:09:33.848
They saw themselves as leading one team

00:09:33.872 --> 00:09:36.676
that was responsible for
the safety of the flight.

00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:37.956
The ineffective captains

00:09:37.980 --> 00:09:40.766
reinforced fault lines between subgroups.

00:09:40.790 --> 00:09:44.521
They called the pilots
"we" but everyone else "you."

00:09:48.550 --> 00:09:49.884
This lack of shared identity

00:09:49.908 --> 00:09:52.194
hurts the work of face-to-face colleagues

00:09:52.218 --> 00:09:55.386
but creates an even bigger problem
for remote teams.

00:09:55.410 --> 00:09:57.126
MH: It reduces trust.

00:09:57.150 --> 00:09:59.786
It reduces psychological safety,

00:09:59.810 --> 00:10:03.146
that sense that it's safe to
kind of speak up in the group.